From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:31:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] virgl: fill in the size of an exported dmabuf

virgl_drm_winsys_resource_get_handle filled the handle and stride but
left whandle->size at 0, and VADRMPRIMESurfaceDescriptor's object size
is copied straight from it, so a VA-API consumer was told nothing about
how much memory the fd names. Report the BO's size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
index 89fce3bebcf..5b5f6e58f4a 100644
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
@@ -703,6 +703,9 @@ static bool virgl_drm_winsys_resource_get_handle(struct virgl_winsys *qws,
    p_atomic_set(&res->external, true);
 
    whandle->stride = stride;
+   /* VADRMPRIMESurfaceDescriptor.objects[].size is copied straight from here, and left at 0
+    * it tells a consumer nothing about how much memory the fd actually names. */
+   whandle->size = res->size;
    return true;
 }
 
